{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfi6XFfVy6oxDVoUkaUAQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] The core bundle gains no runtime code from this ticket (`npm run size` unchanged for `microtags`)\n\nTicket 01 is finished and committed, and all six checklist items are done. `npm test` passes (181/181). `npm run lint` still fails on two errors that were there before I started (see below).\n\n**What changed:**\n1. `Serialized<T>` is added in `src/types.ts` and exported, with `Signal`, as a type from `src/index.ts`. It's a single mapped type: each signal property becomes its value type, everything else passes through, and nested signals are left alone.\n2. Four checks in `test/types.ts`. They import from `'microtags'`, so they test the public export rather than the source file. Each one covers one ticket item: the import compiles, signals unwrap, plain properties pass through, and nested signals stay as they are. For each, I swapped in a wrong expected type and confirmed the typecheck failed, so they can actually catch a regression.\n3. `docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md` has context, decision, trade-offs and consequences, plus a row in `INDEX.md`. No existing ADR is marked superseded.\n4. The core bundle is 4.01 kB before and after, so no runtime code was added.\n5. A short note in `AGENTS.md`: importing from `'microtags'` in the type tests resolves to `dist/`, so you have to rebuild before typechecking.\n\n**Outside the ticket:**\n- **Test import fix:** `npm test` was already failing at the start. Commit `eeebd71` renamed `example-hydration/client/reveal.ts` to `util.ts`, but `test/index.ts` still imported the old path. I changed that one import path in its own commit (`4744cd8`); without it the final test run couldn't pass.\n- **Lint errors left alone:** `npm run lint` reports two unused-variable errors in `test/plugins.ts` (lines 105 and 214). They were there before this work and that file isn't part of the ticket, so I didn't change it.\n- **Installed dependencies:** the worktree had no `node_modules` and no lockfile, so I ran `npm install`. No tracked files changed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":589,"cache_read_input_tokens":73197,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":589},"output_tokens":714,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99908130-e653-4773-b7a4-9aed1299a569","uuid":"954d03bf-3070-4d6a-acc8-f7a40e946e91","timestamp":"2026-10-04T23:52:18.247Z","request_id":"req_011Cfi6XEyL7DJFERj8dEdw5"}
